# Every text file is LF in the working tree on every OS. Git for Windows ships
# core.autocrlf=true, so a fresh Windows clone (made before home/dot_gitconfig.tmpl
# renders ~/.gitconfig with autocrlf=false) would otherwise get CRLF files that
# then show as modified, and dots sync refuses a dirty tree.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
